1
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:11,634
This is Smart Stock, a web-based
inventory, sales and decision support

2
00:00:11,714 --> 00:00:19,691
system built for A and A Surplus, a Japan
surplus appliance store in Panabo City. It

3
00:00:19,771 --> 00:00:25,734
runs in a browser on the shop's own
machine, keeps stock records in step with

4
00:00:25,814 --> 00:00:32,113
every sale, and warns the office before
popular items run out.

5
00:00:32,663 --> 00:00:39,149
Access is role-based. Every person signs
in with their own account, and what they

6
00:00:39,229 --> 00:00:45,118
see afterwards depends on the job they do.
The note under the heading is not

7
00:00:45,198 --> 00:00:52,281
decoration: every action in this system is
written to an audit trail against the

8
00:00:52,361 --> 00:00:54,370
account that performed it.

9
00:00:58,518 --> 00:01:07,161
Signed in as an administrator, the
dashboard opens on the figures the office

10
00:01:07,241 --> 00:01:15,126
needs. Sales so far today, revenue for the
month, the number of pieces on the floor

11
00:01:15,206 --> 00:01:22,332
and what they are worth, and how many
items have fallen to or below their

12
00:01:22,412 --> 00:01:29,917
reorder level. Note the figures as they
stand now. Nothing has been sold today.

13
00:01:30,493 --> 00:01:37,379
Inventory is the main master file.
Thirty-four item types, forty- eight

14
00:01:37,459 --> 00:01:44,677
pieces in total. Because these are
second-hand appliances, every item carries

15
00:01:44,757 --> 00:01:51,311
a condition grade alongside its cost, its
selling price and its own barcode. The

16
00:01:51,391 --> 00:01:57,614
catalogue can be searched and filtered,
and exported to a spreadsheet.

17
00:01:58,185 --> 00:02:07,295
Stock alerts separate the two problems
that matter. Items that are already out of

18
00:02:07,375 --> 00:02:16,485
stock and cannot be sold at all, and items
at or below their reorder level that will

19
00:02:16,565 --> 00:02:24,840
run out soon. Each one carries a restock
action, so the warning leads somewhere.

20
00:02:25,593 --> 00:02:32,374
The reports module covers sales and
revenue, inventory valuation and stock

21
00:02:32,454 --> 00:02:40,171
movement, over any date range. Everything
reads zero at the moment, because no sale

22
00:02:40,251 --> 00:02:44,537
has been recorded today. Watch these
figures later.

23
00:02:44,936 --> 00:02:51,645
Price approvals are how the shop controls
discounting. A member of staff who wants

24
00:02:51,725 --> 00:02:58,433
to drop a price has to ask, and give a
reason. Here, chipped veneer on one chair,

25
00:02:58,513 --> 00:03:05,222
and a desk that has been sitting on the
floor for six weeks. Until a manager

26
00:03:05,302 --> 00:03:11,332
decides, nothing changes, and the decision
is stamped with their name.

27
00:03:13,812 --> 00:03:21,475
Signing out, and back in as a cashier, to
show the same system from the other side

28
00:03:21,555 --> 00:03:22,950
of the counter.

29
00:03:25,192 --> 00:03:32,736
This is the same application, but the
cashier sees a different screen and a

30
00:03:32,816 --> 00:03:39,978
shorter menu. Their own takings for the
day, the pieces that have left the shop,

31
00:03:40,058 --> 00:03:47,983
what is still on the floor, and what is
running low. The administration modules

32
00:03:48,063 --> 00:03:55,607
are not hidden from view here, they are
not available to this account at all.

33
00:03:56,035 --> 00:04:03,323
The point of sale lists the stock as
cards, with a photograph, the condition

34
00:04:03,403 --> 00:04:11,079
grade, the price and how many are left. An
item can be found by searching, or by

35
00:04:11,159 --> 00:04:18,447
scanning the barcode printed on the piece
itself. Notice the green note on the

36
00:04:18,527 --> 00:04:26,591
right: a ten per cent discount has already
been approved by the store manager.

37
00:04:27,006 --> 00:04:33,462
Adding an item builds the sale. The
subtotal is two thousand nine hundred

38
00:04:33,542 --> 00:04:40,651
pesos, the approved discount takes two
hundred and ninety off, and the total

39
00:04:40,731 --> 00:04:46,861
falls to two thousand six hundred and ten.
The code beneath the item is the

40
00:04:46,941 --> 00:04:51,109
individual piece being sold, not just the
product type.

41
00:04:52,355 --> 00:04:58,622
The cashier enters the amount handed over.
Three thousand pesos, and the change due

42
00:04:58,702 --> 00:05:03,457
is worked out immediately: three hundred
and ninety.

43
00:05:04,737 --> 00:05:11,918
Completing the sale produces the receipt.
The invoice number, the cashier's name,

44
00:05:11,998 --> 00:05:18,834
the unit code of the piece sold, the
discount and who approved it. The message

45
00:05:18,914 --> 00:05:26,095
above it is the important part: inventory
has already been updated.

46
00:05:28,575 --> 00:05:36,280
Back on the cashier's dashboard, every
figure has moved. One sale, two thousand

47
00:05:36,360 --> 00:05:43,323
six hundred and ten pesos at this till.
Pieces on the floor have dropped from

48
00:05:43,403 --> 00:05:51,478
forty-eight to forty-seven. The item sold
now shows zero left, and it has appeared

49
00:05:51,558 --> 00:05:58,892
at the top of the running- low list. The
movement log records it against the

50
00:05:58,972 --> 00:06:00,375
invoice number.

51
00:06:04,371 --> 00:06:11,561
The office sees the same thing without
doing anything. Sales today are no longer

52
00:06:11,641 --> 00:06:19,177
zero. Inventory on hand has fallen to
forty-seven, the stock value has dropped

53
00:06:19,257 --> 00:06:26,100
by the cost of the item sold, and the
alert count has risen from eight to nine.

54
00:06:26,180 --> 00:06:31,985
One transaction at the till, and the whole
system is consistent.

55
00:06:34,966 --> 00:06:42,064
The same report that read zero a few
minutes ago now shows the transaction, the

56
00:06:42,144 --> 00:06:49,569
revenue, the average sale value, and the
discount given as a percentage of revenue.

57
00:06:49,649 --> 00:06:56,095
Reports read from the same tables the till
writes to, so they cannot fall out of

58
00:06:56,175 --> 00:06:56,875
date.

59
00:07:02,213 --> 00:07:10,560
This is the decision support the system is
named for. Six months of trading, six

60
00:07:10,640 --> 00:07:18,986
hundred and seventy-two transactions, and
a least- squares trend line extended three

61
00:07:19,066 --> 00:07:27,413
months forward. The solid bars are what
was actually taken. The dashed line is the

62
00:07:27,493 --> 00:07:35,438
projection the office uses to decide what
the next container should carry.

63
00:07:35,872 --> 00:07:42,036
Finally, the audit trail, which has been
recording this demonstration as it

64
00:07:42,116 --> 00:07:48,593
happened. The cashier signing in, the
discount applied and who approved it, the

65
00:07:48,673 --> 00:07:56,086
completed sale with its invoice number and
total, and the administrator signing back

66
00:07:56,166 --> 00:08:00,769
in. Every entry names the account
responsible.

